<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karamanoğlu Mehmed Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1278</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karamanoğlu Mehmed Bey was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaman-bey">Karaman Bey</a>, founder of the Karamanid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus</a> mountains. In 1277 he occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a>, capital of the declining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a>, and is reported to have decreed that Turkish alone be used at court and in government. He was killed fighting Mongol and Seljuk forces in 1278.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karamanoglu-mehmed-bey.jpg" alt="Karamanoğlu Mehmed Bey" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karamanoğlu Ekrem · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karamano%C4%9FluMehmed1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
